Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.66,0:00:05.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward-sama!\NIs something the matter?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.45,0:00:06.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's nothing!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.96,0:00:08.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told them not to disturb us...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.96,0:00:11.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I guess they don't trust you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.13,0:00:15.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'd feel a lot better after revealing who you really are, wouldn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.18,0:00:21.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fletcher!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.52,0:00:27.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Run! Hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.23,0:00:30.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.36,0:00:34.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If they catch you,\Nwe won't get off easily, either!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.82,0:00:36.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In time, I'll clear everything up!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.49,0:00:41.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.38,0:01:00.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry,\NBrother...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.06,0:01:09.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything\Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.73,0:01:14.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything,\Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.98,0:01:19.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's\NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.74,0:01:25.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that\Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.98,0:03:17.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You promised not to use alchemy, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.98,0:03:19.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dad didn't like it, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.61,0:03:24.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Th-This is terrible!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.82,0:03:25.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mugear-sama...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.45,0:03:29.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You two are all right!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.33,0:03:31.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And the stone?\NIs the stone all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.74,0:03:34.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not to worry, it's right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.75,0:03:38.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've done well\Nto make it so large.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.34,0:03:42.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, we don't\Nhave any more time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.30,0:03:44.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please start using\Nthat other method.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.01,0:03:47.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We don't need to use that method for the stone to—
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.18,0:03:51.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you saying you won't follow my orders?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.10,0:03:53.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,N-No...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.60,0:03:57.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There was once another man who told me the same thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.02,0:04:00.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In the end, he ran away,\Nlike a beaten dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.73,0:04:03.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.94,0:04:07.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With this, even without being an alchemist, I can do this!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.71,0:04:17.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mugear-sama!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.37,0:04:19.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Magnificent!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.54,0:04:25.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The real Elric brothers are said to\Nhave blond hair and golden eyes,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.84,0:04:28.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,sons of Nash Tringham!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.69,0:04:42.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Things have sure been bustling over at the mansion, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.86,0:04:44.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, really?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.07,0:04:48.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You went there again, huh?\NThere's no helping you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.16,0:04:52.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Is Elisa still here?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.32,0:04:53.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.24,0:04:57.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The grapevine is withering,\Nso she wanted to stay here, and she won't listen to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.29,0:05:00.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But her cough is terrible.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.29,0:05:02.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I just put her down.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.01,0:05:07.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Red water?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.42,0:05:10.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're condensing it,\Ntrying to turn it into a stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.18,0:05:13.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then again, compared to the Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.51,0:05:16.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the red-water piece is\Njust a pale imitation.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.14,0:05:19.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you suppose he meant by "his father's dream"?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.02,0:05:22.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Probably just some goofy excuse.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.56,0:05:24.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Could it be that those two are...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.44,0:05:25.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nash's sons?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.36,0:05:27.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nash?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.86,0:05:31.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean Nash Tringham,\Nthe discoverer of the red water?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.86,0:05:34.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He was from this town.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.12,0:05:37.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He went to Central to\Nresearch the red water.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.20,0:05:41.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then, one day, \Nhe came back to this town.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.96,0:05:48.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nash? Well, if it isn't Nash!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.55,0:05:50.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've returned, huh?\NHow are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.05,0:05:56.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This town is completely\Non the decline.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.64,0:06:00.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I think we should stop relying on gold for our way of life.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.81,0:06:05.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How's your research\Non the red water?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.56,0:06:06.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is it coming along?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.73,0:06:10.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I gave up.\NI'll never research it again.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.49,0:06:13.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not going back to Central, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.95,0:06:15.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.32,0:06:16.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What about your family?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.53,0:06:21.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm a failure,\Nboth as a husband and a father.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.33,0:06:24.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nash...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.04,0:06:28.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He'd abandoned everything he had.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.84,0:06:32.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He wouldn't tell me anything about what happened in Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.05,0:06:39.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then the big landowner in \Nthis town—Mugear—came calling.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.22,0:06:43.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He approached Nash about\Nhis research on the red water.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.44,0:06:49.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No matter how many times you come see me, my answer is the same!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.15,0:06:52.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're saying you'd turn your back on this town?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.53,0:06:56.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right now, the only thing that can produce gold is your red water!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.99,0:06:59.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As long as we have gold,\Nthe town will come back to life!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.45,0:07:04.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nash-san, you're the only one \Nwho can save this town! Please!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.96,0:07:11.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In the end, he secluded himself inside Mugear's mine, and began to research.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.17,0:07:17.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The town once again flourished because of the gold.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.47,0:07:21.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The furnaces were aflame, goods filled the streets,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.60,0:07:25.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and life returned to the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.35,0:07:30.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, at the same time, an illness of unknown origin began to spread.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.78,0:07:38.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Without anyone knowing\Nhow to treat it,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.74,0:07:44.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,many, many babies\Ndied soon after birth.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.83,0:07:49.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And Elisa was born around then?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.71,0:07:56.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shortly, an alchemist doctor named Marcoh wandered into town.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.22,0:08:06.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The cause of this is a toxic material called \Nred water, which has seeped into the ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.11,0:08:15.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It glowed?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.53,0:08:17.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.45,0:08:20.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That light... Could it have been...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.53,0:08:26.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In any case, we can be sure that\Nthanks to his treatment, Elisa survived.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.71,0:08:29.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hounded Nash.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.67,0:08:32.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Answer me, Nash!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.29,0:08:34.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If this keeps up, this will become a town of death!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.00,0:08:36.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What the hell have you done?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.76,0:08:39.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was in the wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.05,0:08:43.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Again... Once again...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.68,0:08:47.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to end it all.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.56,0:08:49.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,End it...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.40,0:08:52.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nash...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.86,0:08:56.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After that, no one\Never saw him again.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.07,0:08:59.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gradually, they couldn't get any more gold,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.28,0:09:01.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and the town once again declined.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.70,0:09:06.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If those two are Nash's sons,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.04,0:09:09.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,they must have come after their father.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.92,0:09:11.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.83,0:09:12.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.42,0:09:14.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They had no choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.96,0:09:17.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The only thing those two have is their father.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.42,0:09:21.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're just using their pop as\Njustification for what they're doing.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.97,0:09:23.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maybe so...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.26,0:09:26.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But aren't we doing\Nsomething similar?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.60,0:09:32.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know how those two feel.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.32,0:09:43.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For crying out loud!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.66,0:09:46.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All you had to do was shut up\Nand use that other method...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.24,0:09:49.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother? What method does he mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.79,0:09:51.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's simple, really.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.83,0:09:55.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Have newly pregnant women drink the red water.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.84,0:09:58.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Soon, the water will pass through the placenta and condense...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.01,0:10:00.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.92,0:10:00.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.01,0:10:04.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the right time, you get it from them and transmute it into a stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.35,0:10:08.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a simple, reliable method.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.27,0:10:16.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My, my, you've got the same sissy streak as your father.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.31,0:10:16.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.02,0:10:18.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I just want you to\Ntell me one thing!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.57,0:10:22.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did Dad use that method?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.11,0:10:27.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hmph, at the last moment, he weaseled out.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.53,0:10:30.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If only he had done it,\Nhis life would've been spared.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.16,0:10:32.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.16,0:10:33.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You said\NDad died from illness!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.29,0:10:36.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.25,0:10:37.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.05,0:10:41.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've taken care of everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.84,0:10:47.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now we just have to use the real Elric brothers and put everything into action.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.56,0:10:52.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I doubt it will go that smoothly.\NThey can be very difficult to deal with.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.93,0:10:56.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,One or two kids won't be any\Ntrouble at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.06,0:10:58.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now, please wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.23,0:11:00.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please wait for\Njust a while longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.36,0:11:03.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Very well. Go on.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.12,0:11:10.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}The time for this place is nigh.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.50,0:11:16.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}I'm so sorry about\Nthose two impostors.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.63,0:11:20.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I, too, was completely\Ntaken in by them.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.63,0:11:24.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I feel terrible about\Nadding to our impertinence,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.72,0:11:27.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but seeing as how the two of you are among the finest alchemists of our age,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.84,0:11:30.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there is a matter that I would like to request your assistance with.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.39,0:11:32.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Research on the red water?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.22,0:11:34.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh! You know about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.77,0:11:36.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That will save me time explaining.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.19,0:11:39.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The truth is, I happened to overhear
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.69,0:11:43.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that you are greatly interested in the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.40,0:11:46.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.70,0:11:51.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was made by condensing the red water.\NYou might call it a trial product for a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.87,0:11:53.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What am I supposed\Nto do with it now?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.70,0:11:56.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I want to save Xenotime.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.33,0:11:59.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I can regenerate the gold vein,\Nno one will have to give up on this town!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.54,0:12:02.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.67,0:12:04.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, where are the impostors?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.92,0:12:06.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're being held in\Nan underground cell.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.22,0:12:11.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wh-What are you doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.85,0:12:14.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not interested in\Nany unfinished goods.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.14,0:12:16.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Executing the impostors comes first.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.98,0:12:19.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not the type of person who forgives liars.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.52,0:12:20.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.69,0:12:22.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then you're accepting my request?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.15,0:12:26.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With us working on it,\Nthis will be child's play.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.24,0:12:28.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Never mind that, I haven't\Nexecuted anyone in a while!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.66,0:12:30.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm just itching for the chance!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.91,0:12:31.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gonna come watch?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.20,0:12:34.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, I, uh...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.91,0:12:37.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll pass on that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.59,0:12:44.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.42,0:12:48.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.34,0:12:49.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alphonse-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.14,0:12:54.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard that Nash Tringham was your pop.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.64,0:12:57.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What were you trying to do by carrying on his research?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.10,0:13:03.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That...\Nis Dad's water.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.86,0:13:06.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was my duty to\Ncontinue his research.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.94,0:13:09.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You are such a naïve bastard.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.82,0:13:14.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you know what the people in town are going through because of that toxic water?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.70,0:13:17.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your pop knew.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.45,0:13:19.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why he tried to\Ngive up his research.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.33,0:13:25.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't obtain happiness by relying on the likes of red water or a Philosopher's Stone!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.51,0:13:31.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Move forward!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.97,0:13:33.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't act so shamefully!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.60,0:13:36.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not now that you've\Ntaken on my name.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.68,0:13:37.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al! Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.15,0:13:45.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who cares?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.48,0:13:48.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As long as the research is successful, those guys will be—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.32,0:13:50.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those guys?\NWho are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.45,0:13:53.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Something's been bothering me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.62,0:13:57.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wherever did the red-water \Nresearcher Nash Tringham go?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.25,0:14:03.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nash? Ah, his research wasn't going so well, so I fired him.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.92,0:14:05.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.21,0:14:09.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't seem like someone\Nso good-natured as to let somebody\Nwho knew everything\Nget away from you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.13,0:14:13.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you trying to say?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.39,0:14:17.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm saying that I don't help murderers out, Mugear!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.93,0:14:19.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.39,0:14:22.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, you're not\Ngetting out of here alive!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.81,0:14:25.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can get any number of\Nother alchemists instead!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.90,0:14:26.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A stone?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.82,0:14:28.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There wasn't just that one?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.94,0:14:31.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It may not be as complete as that other one...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.45,0:14:36.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Die!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.58,0:14:40.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you done yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.66,0:14:43.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.25,0:14:47.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's plenty more\Nwhere that came from!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.67,0:14:51.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're kidding!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.47,0:15:01.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's useless! Useless!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.06,0:15:08.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Equivalent exchange, my ass! Dammit!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.86,0:15:13.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not done yet!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.53,0:15:16.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.12,0:15:21.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now, Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.92,0:15:33.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.92,0:15:36.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Looks like you needed my help after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.34,0:15:37.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.51,0:15:42.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've given up\Nchasing after our dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.77,0:15:46.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're going to go\Nfind our own way.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.31,0:15:49.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.32,0:15:52.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.90,0:15:56.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A secret passage?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.86,0:15:58.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That bastard, he got away!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.99,0:16:03.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Russell, how much farther?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.41,0:16:04.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're almost there!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.66,0:16:06.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a spring where the red water comes out!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.88,0:16:13.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That miserable Mugear! He blocked our way!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.01,0:16:15.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna drag him out of there!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.43,0:16:21.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.27,0:16:26.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll never surrender the spring!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.98,0:16:29.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As long as I have this water, I can continue researching!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.06,0:16:33.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not afraid of\Nany State Alchemist!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.61,0:16:36.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed!\NBrother!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.19,0:16:37.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now you've said it, Mugear!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.07,0:16:40.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't you mock the State Alchemists!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.32,0:16:42.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Die!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.63,0:16:51.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you see now?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.25,0:16:54.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm on an entirely\Ndifferent level than you!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.05,0:16:59.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.01,0:17:05.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed! That's enough!\NLet's get out of here!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.06,0:17:06.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.52,0:17:12.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't give up this spring!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.08,0:17:27.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's the water!\NThe red water is overflowing!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.42,0:17:35.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That should hold it for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.30,0:17:36.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are the other places all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.71,0:17:40.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The bedrock will be unstable after that shock.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.26,0:17:41.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.61,0:18:00.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now, if we can just\Nstop it from coming out...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.97,0:18:29.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The trees...\NThey're absorbing the red water!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.43,0:18:32.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, these kinds of trees\Nwere in the laboratory as well!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.35,0:18:36.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You had them absorb the red water to detoxify it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.57,0:18:41.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.10,0:19:12.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those guys did it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.23,0:19:20.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.98,0:19:22.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.15,0:20:08.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here. These are from Belsio-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.45,0:20:10.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.33,0:20:12.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Big Brother, take care!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.12,0:20:13.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come see us again!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.87,0:20:17.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Mm-hmm, we'll come again for sure!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.18,0:20:17.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You sure you can get by in this town?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.98,0:20:17.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Really? Promise?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.00,0:20:20.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll accept whatever's coming to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.00,0:20:23.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Okay, let's do a parting handshake!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.25,0:20:23.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Working with Belsio-san, my powers will be useful.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.63,0:20:29.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed, are you still going to search for the Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.63,0:20:29.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Wow, you're so big!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.18,0:20:35.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.23,0:20:40.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look, how about I tell you \Nhow to condense a red stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.67,0:20:41.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.11,0:20:43.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not by way of apology,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.23,0:20:47.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it's just that I think\Nyou should know.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.57,0:20:52.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We don't need that stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.08,0:20:55.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll find it on our own.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.50,0:20:56.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Count on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.12,0:20:59.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed-san! Please come again!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.33,0:21:00.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're sure to make this town better!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.13,0:21:04.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When you do, Big Brother,\Nbe taller, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.75,0:21:07.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?! Why, you!\NThat wasn't very nice!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.35,0:21:17.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good-bye!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.56,0:21:18.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Bye-bye!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.00,0:21:21.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good-bye!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.81,0:21:24.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good-bye!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.20,0:21:38.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A letter, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.20,0:21:39.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A letter?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.37,0:21:41.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. What could it be?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.71,0:21:45.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.05,0:21:47.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I-It's nothing!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.17,0:21:51.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Show me! Show me!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.97,0:21:53.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Show me!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.68,0:21:56.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Show me, already!\NCome on, Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.10,0:21:57.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}"Ed,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.72,0:22:00.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}thanks for all your help."
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.39,0:22:04.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}"Being a year younger than you,\NI'm sorry I was such a smart-aleck."
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.82,0:22:08.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}"I'm trying to be a better\Nolder brother to Fletcher,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.49,0:22:11.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I'll try hard to follow your example, Ed."
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.07,0:22:14.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}"Well, have a nice trip."\N{\i1}"Russell."
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.20,0:22:17.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Damn, how can he be younger than me,\Nand still be taller?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.79,0:22:22.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What a joke!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.08,0:22:24.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those two are going\Nto be all right, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:25.04,0:22:25.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.63,0:22:29.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They had a nice,\Nresolute look on their faces.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.70,0:23:40.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.41,0:23:43.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 13: "Flame VS Fullmetal"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.79,0:23:46.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel Roy Mustang, State Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.92,0:23:48.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Title: "Flame."
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.58,0:23:50.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's probably stronger than Brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.59,0:23:51.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, no he's not!
